---
import ContentSection from "~/components/content-section.astro";
---

<ContentSection title="A Letter to Readers" id="letter">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="bg-offset border border-default rounded-lg p-8 md:p-12 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed italic">
      <p class="font-serif italic text-xl">Dear Reader,</p>

      <p>You read, think, and ask AI in the browser. But real work gets messy: too many tabs, half-written prompts, copy-paste across windows, and lost focus. Our sidebar exists to fix that—<strong>a temporary scratchpad that lives next to the page you're reading.</strong></p>

      <div class="my-8">
        <h3 class="text-primary font-bold text-xl mb-4">What problem does it solve?</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
          <li>Prompts need iteration, but context switching breaks your train of thought.</li>
          <li>Useful lines on the page are far from where you write.</li>
          <li>Raw, rushed prompts lead to vague answers.</li>
          <li>Quick ideas disappear because there's no light-weight place to hold them.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="my-8">
        <h3 class="text-primary font-bold text-xl mb-4">How it helps</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
          <li><strong>Capture instantly:</strong> Select text and hit a hotkey to send it to the sidebar.</li>
          <li><strong>Think in one place:</strong> Notes, fragments, and prompts stay beside the source.</li>
          <li><strong>Shape better prompts:</strong> Refine in small passes until the question is clear.</li>
          <li><strong>Stay in flow:</strong> Keyboard-first; no jumping between apps.</li>
          <li><strong>Move on cleanly:</strong> Keep it while you're working; export or discard when done.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="my-8">
        <h3 class="text-primary font-bold text-xl mb-4">When to use it</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
          <li><strong>Researching an article:</strong> grab key lines, draft a precise question, ask the model, collect the best answer back in the pad.</li>
          <li><strong>Drafting:</strong> outline in bullets, tighten the prompt, iterate once or twice, paste the result where it belongs.</li>
          <li><strong>Debugging or reading docs:</strong> pin error messages or API snippets, form a targeted query, record the fix.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="my-8">
        <h3 class="text-primary font-bold text-xl mb-4">What it is (and isn't)</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
          <li>It <strong>is</strong> a professional, short-term buffer for focused thinking.</li>
          <li>It <strong>is not</strong> a long-term notebook or knowledge base.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p><strong>In short:</strong> one small place to capture, refine, and act—so your prompts are sharper, your answers better, and your attention intact. Use it as the quiet companion to your chat-based AI, and let the work proceed without friction.</p>

    </div>
  </div>
</ContentSection>
